{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Larger tiles are a major improvement: the best local timings so far are around `0.57 ms` on a representative `B=4, S=512` shape, down from `2.6 ms` in the first verifier run and closer to the `0.45 ms` reference. I’m letting the tile sweep finish and then I’ll update the kernel to use the best stable settings."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The best large-shape tile is `128x256x64`, but that creates too few programs for short sequences. I’m benchmarking a small set of candidate tiles across the actual workload shapes and will dispatch by `M = batch * seq` rather than using one tile everywhere."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, torch, triton, time\nfrom kernel import _proj_kernel\nwork=[]\nfor line in open('workload.jsonl'):\n    j=json.loads(line); work.append((j['axes']['batch_size'], j['axes']['seq_len']))\n# representative candidates\nconfigs=[\n('16x64x128',(16,64,128,4,3)),\n('16x128x64',(16,128,64,8,3)),\n('32x64x64',(32,64,64,4,3)),\n('32x128x64',(32,128,64,4,3)),\n('64x64x64',(64,64,64,4,3)),\n('64x128x64',(64,128,64,4,3)),\n('64x256x64',(64,256,64,8,3)),\n('128x128x64s2',(128,128,64,4,2)),\n('128x256x32',(128,256,32,8,3)),\n('128x256x64',(128,256,64,8,3)),\n]\n\ndef bench(B,S,cfg,iters=5):\n    BM,BN,BK,warps,stages=cfg\n    M=B*S; N=7168; K=16384\n    attn=torch.randn((B,128,S,128), device='cuda', dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n    w=torch.randn((N,K), device='cuda', dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n    out=torch.empty((B,S,N), device='cuda', dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n    grid=(triton.cdiv(M,BM), triton.cdiv(N,BN))\n    for _ in range(2):\n        _proj_kernel[grid](attn,w,out,M,S,N,K,BLOCK_M=BM,BLOCK_N=BN,BLOCK_K=BK,num_warps=warps,num_stages=stages)\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    st=torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True); en=torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True)\n    st.record()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        _proj_kernel[grid](attn,w,out,M,S,N,K,BLOCK_M=BM,BLOCK_N=BN,BLOCK_K=BK,num_warps=warps,num_stages=stages)\n    en.record(); torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    return st.elapsed_time(en)/iters\n\nfor idx,(B,S) in enumerate(work):\n    print(f'work {idx} B={B} S={S} M={B*S}')\n    best=(999,None)\n    for name,cfg in configs:\n        try:\n            ms=bench(B,S,cfg,iters=3)\n            if ms<best[0]: best=(ms,name)\n            print(f'  {name:14s} {ms:.3f}')\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f'  {name:14s} ERR {type(e).__name__} {str(e)[:70]}')\n    print('  BEST',best[1],f'{best[0]:.3f}')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
